/A 1389 0 R
/Alt (Fig. 4. Distantly supervised learning. In this approach, facts in a structured knowledge representation are projected onto pieces of text that mention the people, places, dates, etc., that appear in knowledge-base entries.This projection is noisy, but when done over large quantities of text, it provides enough signal to successfully learn good classifiers for extracting relations from text. [Photo source:National Library of Australia] ␀)
